            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Six String Sidekick 0.2.0 (26)</h2>
<h3>New in builds 25 and 26</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Guitar or Bass, throughout the app:</b> switch on Home, from the instrument control at the top of tool screens, or from the Mac Instrument menu. Bass supports 4, 5 or 6 strings, bass tunings, correctly sized fretboards and tab staves, and root, fifth, octave and arpeggio positions in Chord Finder.</li>
<li><b>Microphone tuner:</b> guitar and bass tuning presets, including bass Drop D, with pitch detection down to low B.</li>
<li><b>Chord Progression Builder:</b> choose a key and style, tap chords to build a progression, use Suggest for familiar patterns, and see what fits next. Transpose, view capo shapes, loop playback at 60–180 bpm, copy the progression, or save it into a song. Works with Guitar or Bass.</li>
<li><b>Updated offline Help and User Manual</b> cover both new tools and the instrument switch. Existing songs stay unchanged; the app starts on Guitar.</li>
</ul>
<p>Requires macOS 14 or newer. Universal for Apple Silicon and Intel. This personal test build is ad-hoc signed, not Apple-notarized. Microphone tuning and progression playback have automated coverage but still need real-instrument and speaker listening checks.</p>
]]></description>
